TI  - CONSUMPTION OF FISH FATS AND ITS EFFECTS ON PLASMATIC LIPIDS
T2  - REVISTA CLINICA ESPANOLA
AB  - The low incidence of coronary disease in populations with a high intake of omega 3 (w-3) fatty acids has lead us to study the efects of fish fat consumption (that is fish rich in these fatty acids) on plasmatic lipids. For this purpose we have sellected a population with IIb and IV type hyperlipidemias. During tow months each patients received a diet rich in fatty acids w-3 (1 gr/day of eicosapentenoic as acid and docosahexaenoic acid). We determined cholesterol, triglicerides and lipoproteins.  Significant drops in the triglicerides and VLDL-cholesterol values were observed but no statistically significant variations were observed in the rest of the parameters. Hence we feel that the consumption of fish fats in normal diets is recomendable because of the beneficial efects on plasmatic lipids.
