T2  - EVERYMANS SCIENCE
AB  - Seafood is the single most important food we can eat for good health. Regular consumption may help to increase intelligence, reduce the risk of various diseases and disorders. Fish is rich in omega-3 fatty acids which are known to contribute for the healthy development of brain tissue and retina in children. Eating of fish reduces the risk of heart disease and stroke by reducing blood clots and inflammation, improving blood vessel elasticity, lowering blood pressure, lowering blood fats and boosting good cholesterol. This article deals with the different nutraceuticals obtained from the fish and shellfish and their applications in different areas.
