TI  - CHANGES IN ACUTE RELEASE OF T-PA AFTER CHRONIC ADMINISTRATION OF N-3 POLYUNSATURATED FATTY-ACIDS INTO RABBITS
T2  - FIBRINOLYSIS
CP  - Leiden Fibrinolysis Workshop 5: Intervention in Fibrinolysis
AB  - The oral administration of a fish oil to rabbits leads to a decrease of the tissue-type plasminogen activator (t-PA) activity in plasma. Tn order to investigate the possible causes of this effect a fish oil was fed during 4 weeks to rabbits and after that t-PA release was provoked by the intravenous injection of epinephrine. Control animals were injected by epinephrine without a pretreatment by a fish oil. The t-PA liberator injection caused a significant, but a transient, increase in t-PA activity both in the fish oil-treated and untreated animals. Although the basal activity of t-PA in the fish oil-treated animals was smaller than in control rabbits, the release of this enzyme after drug stimulation was higher in this group as compared to the untreated animals. At 30 min after injection of epinephrine t-PA activity in the experimental animals was less than in control rabbits.
